    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d45">

                <pb facs="0144" n="898" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v02/pg898"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/3980</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 6451</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-06-22">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 22, 1917</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received July 6.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that on June
                    19, 1917 (copy of letter attached<anchor n="2" xml:id="d45-f1"/>), Sir Adam Block requested Mr.
                        Beal of my staff to attend a meeting to be held at the
                    office of the Ministry of Blockade on June 21, 1917, to consider a proposal to
                    tighten the financial blockade of the enemy by obtaining general assurances from
                    neutral banks that they will restrict their business within certain limits and
                    confine their operations to transacting such business with the enemy as will not
                    injure the Allies, as a condition of continuing their financial relations with
                    Allied countries.</p>
                <pb facs="0145" n="899" xml:id="pg899"/>
                <p>In accordance with Sir Adam
                        Block’s invitation, Mr. Beal went to this
                    meeting, which was also attended by representatives of the French, Russian and
                    Italian Governments, and I enclose herewith, for your information a copy of the
                    minutes, together with a copy of the suggestions (Exhibit A) made by Sir Adam Block at that time. I
                    also enclose herewith copy of further suggestions (Exhibit B),<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d45-f2"/> which Sir
                        Adam Block has since had written out and which have just been
                    received by Mr. Beal.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Walter Hines Page</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d45-a1.xml" xpointer="d45-a1"/>
